{"id": "EUVD-2026-93391", "enisaUuid": "40a3dd27-4258-3ea3-8cb8-bb9b19a4641a", "description": "libmikmod before 3.3.14 contains an integer overflow in the Oktalyzer loader OKT_doPBOD() that allows attackers to cause heap buffer overflow via crafted track counts. Attackers can supply an OKT module whose SLEN chunk wraps the 16-bit numtrk value, causing PBOD writes past allocated track pointers for crashes or code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T13:35:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T16:12:22", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sezero/mikmod/commit/097b69281fad6ba38a553569e6f55dbfdd71dc2a", "https://github.com/sezero/mikmod/blob/libmikmod-3.3.13/libmikmod/loaders/load_okt.c#L286", "https://github.com/sezero/mikmod/blob/libmikmod-3.3.14/libmikmod/NEWS", "https://github.com/sezero/mikmod", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libmikmod-before-3.3.14-heap-buffer-overflow-via-okt-loader-okt-dopbod"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w386-36c3-r8wv", "CVE-2026-105839"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b43651d7-7030-34f2-b9bb-77db2a85ef02", "product": {"name": "libmikmod", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.3.14"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b878ff5c-9a0b-393b-affe-942d312c9441", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}], "isExploited": false}